  <h1>How to Fix T3T App Login &amp; OTP Problems</h1>  
  <p>If you are not receiving the one-time password (OTP) or experiencing login failure when signing in to the T3T App, follow these quick solutions.</p>  

  <h2>Common Fixes for Missing OTPs</h2>  
  <div class="card">  
    <h3>1. Check Spam &amp; Blocked Messages</h3>  
    <p>Many Android devices with Truecaller or Google Messages automatically divert automated SMS shortcodes into the <strong>Spam and Blocked</strong> folder. Check your SMS spam archive.</p>  
  </div>  

  <div class="card">  
    <h3>2. Wait for 60-Second Timer Before Resending</h3>  
    <p>Repeatedly tapping "Resend OTP" flags the SMS gateway for rate limiting. Wait out the 60-second cooldown timer, check that your SIM has network bars, and request again.</p>  
  </div>  

  <div class="card">  
    <h3>3. Clear App Cache Data</h3>  
    <p>Go to your phone's <strong>Settings → Apps → T3T → Storage</strong> and tap <strong>Clear Cache</strong>. Restart your device to refresh communication tokens.</p>  
  </div>  

  <div class="card">  
    <h3>4. Verify Country Prefix</h3>  
    <p>Ensure you enter your 10-digit Indian mobile number without typing an extra <code>+91</code> or leading zero <code>0</code>, as the system appends the country code automatically.</p>  
  </div>  

